<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 560 0 R
/E (CXS is a high-speed, low-latency, streaming interface protocol mainly used for die-to-die communication, NoC connectivity, and chiplet architectures. It is designed to move large amounts of data efficiently between blocks, IPs, or chiplets, similar in nature to AMBA CHI streaming, AXI-Stream, or PIPE interfaces.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [2]
>>
